# GEO raw/source data
# Expression matrices ARE tracked, but only as gzip-compressed .csv.gz
# (verified byte-identical to the uncompressed .csv via SHA-256; GSE135251's
# compressed size, ~39MB, clears GitHub's 100MB per-file limit that the
# uncompressed 123MB original did not). Only the uncompressed .csv is
# excluded here -- this pattern does not match *.csv.gz.
data/geo_cohorts/*expression_matrix.csv
data/geo_cohorts/*_Gene_counts_raw.txt.gz
data/geo_cohorts/*_family.soft.gz
data/geo_cohorts/*_RAW.tar

# Human-GEM base model (large, regenerable via scripts/01_load_base_model.py)
models/Human-GEM.xml
models/Human-GEM.json

# Python caches / virtual environments
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.pyo
.venv/
venv/
env/
ENV/

# IDE / OS files
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# logs
logs/
audit/logs/
*.log

# temporary / debug files
scripts/_test_*.log
scripts/watch_imat_*.csv
data/context_specific_models/_fastcc_consistent_set.json
tINIT_test.lp
audit/details/dmahdi_literal_string_search.txt
*.tmp

# backup directories
scripts/_backups/
data/*/_backup_pre_*/

# credentials / secrets
*.env
*credentials*
*api_key*
*.pem

# private manuscript/document files
GEM1_manuscript_post-audit.docx
JBI/

# environment-specific tool config
.claude/

# generated bulk sampling intermediates (summary.csv/validation.json/manifest kept)
data/flux_sampling/*samples.csv.gz

# paired-counterfactual production: raw per-background x per-reaction pair
# shards (~335MB across all 10 groups, ~20.7M rows) AND the 8,000 individual
# per-background summary CSVs (~2.7MB, 800 files/group x 10 groups) are both
# bulk Monte-Carlo-draw-level intermediates -- excluded, same policy as
# data/flux_sampling/*samples.csv.gz above. The derived reaction_scores.csv
# (final per-group output), manifest.json, and checkpoint.json are kept.
data/paired_perturbation_production/*/pairs/
data/paired_perturbation_production/*/backgrounds/

# paired-counterfactual pilot: same policy, raw per-seed pair/background
# shards excluded, derived reaction_scores.csv and small summary CSVs kept.
data/paired_perturbation_pilot/*__pairs.csv.gz
data/paired_perturbation_pilot/*__backgrounds.csv

# old (superseded) unpaired-perturbation N-ladder convergence sweep: raw
# intermediate only. The reproducibility-failure finding it investigates is
# independently documented in audit/ (already tracked); this raw sweep data
# is not itself a manuscript result.
data/perturbation_pilot/

# redundant archive bundle (contents already tracked individually elsewhere)
GEM1_project_package.zip

# ad hoc local backup/handoff artifacts -- not part of the repository
# structure (zip/rar snapshots of directories already tracked individually;
# a personal cross-session continuity note, not project documentation).
# No legitimate repository output is a .zip/.rar, so excluded globally --
# new ones have kept appearing during this session (e.g.
# data/paired_perturbation_statistics/tables.zip,
# .../figures/figF_source_data.zip), apparently created outside this
# session's own actions.
*.zip
*.rar
GEM1_handoff.md

# stray file with a malformed/truncated name (embedded commas, ".not.txt"
# suffix) -- appears to be an accidental duplicate of
# scripts/proposed_pilot_reaction_subset_v2.csv, not a real input
scripts/reaction_id,component,old_score,not.txt

# Claude Code tooling config -- CLAUDE.md at this path is actually a stub for the
# shared parent directory (D:\Mahdi), not GEM1 project documentation: it contains
# Claude-Code-internal meta-instructions, references to a personal .claude.json,
# and machine-specific paths (D:/Mahdi/GEM1, D:/Mahdi/ferroptosis). CLAUDE.md.bak
# is an internal development artifact (an old, stale snapshot of GEM1's actual
# project memory). Neither belongs in the public release.
CLAUDE.md
CLAUDE.md.bak

# bootstrap prompt for starting a Claude Code session on this project --
# entirely dependent on CLAUDE.md (see above), which is not part of the
# public release, so this file would only point readers at a nonexistent file
KICKOFF_PROMPT.md

# development/diagnostic scripts not required by the publication/reproducibility pipeline
# (kept locally, just not part of the public release -- see audit/README.md Phase 6 report)
scripts/_*.py
!scripts/_floor_sensitivity_check.py
# paired-counterfactual post-production statistics/figure package: real,
# cited manuscript outputs (data/paired_perturbation_statistics/,
# data/paired_perturbation_synthesis/), same rationale as
# _floor_sensitivity_check.py above -- kept despite the underscore-prefix
# dev-script naming convention.
!scripts/_paired_perturbation_synthesis.py
!scripts/_stats_core_analysis.py
!scripts/_fig_A_architecture.py
!scripts/_fig_B_positive_effect.py
!scripts/_fig_C_recurrence_null.py
!scripts/_fig_D_cross_cohort.py
!scripts/_fig_E_biomarker_heatmap.py
!scripts/_fig_F_pilot_mc.py
scripts/_run_step7_then_step8.ps1
scripts/diagnose_and_run.ps1
